  "id": "COMPOUND:20322 - PROTEIN:890",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 1,3-Diphenylpropan-1-One may interact with Carbonic anhydrase 4 through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is linked to Sodium channel protein type 11 subunit alpha, which in turn targets Amidepsine D, and Amidepsine D further targets Carbonic anhydrase 4. Similarly, 1,3-Diphenylpropan-1-One is also associated with DNA gyrase subunit B, which is targeted by Longispinogenin, which also targets Carbonic anhydrase 4. These pathways highlight a potential mechanism where the drug influences cellular processes through different molecular targets, ultimately leading to the inhibition of Carbonic anhydrase 4. The integration of these targets suggests a broader role for 1,3-Diphenylpropan-1-One in modulating cellular functions, possibly through distinct pathways that converge on the same downstream effect. The evidence supports a complex, multi-target interaction network, where the drug may exert its effects by influencing various cellular processes that ultimately lead to the inhibition of Carbonic anhydrase 4.",
